    "## `simulation.py`\n",
    "\n",
    "Core logic of CMR:\n",
    "- simulates single trials of encoding and retrieval\n",
    "- provides batch wrappers for running multiple simulations with or without diagnostic tracking."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b3590169",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## `simulate_single_trial`\n",
    "\n",
    "Simulates exactly one list of $N$ items being studied and subsequently recalled. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c3b28604",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Encoding pseudocode\n",
    "* Initialize the context vector $c$ to an empty state.\n",
    "* Initialize the Feature-to-Context ($M_{FC}$) and Context-to-Feature ($M_{CF}$) weight matrices.\n",
    "* **For each item $i$ in the presentation list:**\n",
    "  * Formulate the input context $c_{in}$ based on the item's features.\n",
    "  * Update the context vector $c$ by drifting it towards $c_{in}$, scaled by the encoding drift rate ($B_{enc} \\times B_{encD\\_scale}$).\n",
    "  * Update $M_{FC}$ to associate the item's features with the current context $c$ (governed by $\\gamma_{fc}$).\n",
    "  * Update $M_{CF}$ to associate the current context $c$ with the item's features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e5192b64",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Implementation\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Initialize the context vector $c$ to an empty state.**\n",
    "\n",
    "    | $c_0 = [1, 0, 0, \\dots]^T$ | `c = np.zeros((N + 2, 1))`<br>`c[0, 0] = 1.0` |\n",
    "    | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "\n",
    "<br>\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Initialize the Feature-to-Context ($M_{FC}$) and Context-to-Feature ($M_{CF}$) weight matrices.**\n",
    "\n",
    "    | $M_{FC} = 0$<br>$M_{CF} = 0$ | `net_w_fc = np.zeros((N + 2, N + 2))`<br>`net_w_cf = np.zeros((N + 2, N + 2))` |\n",
    "    | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "\n",
    "<br>\n",
    "\n",
    "* **For each item $i$ in the presentation list:**\n",
    "\n",
    "    * **Formulate the input context $c_{in}$ based on the item's features.**\n",
    "\n",
    "        | $c_{in} = f_i$ | `f_in = np.zeros((N + 2, 1))`<br>`f_in[idx + 1] = 1.0`<br>`c_in = f_in` |\n",
    "        | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "\n",
    "    <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "    * **Update the context vector $c$ by drifting it towards $c_{in}$, scaled by the encoding drift rate ($\\beta_{enc} \\times B_{encD\\_scale}$).**\n",
    "\n",
    "        | $\\rho = \\sqrt{1 - \\beta_{enc}^2}$<br>$c_i = \\rho \\cdot c_{i-1} + \\beta_{enc} \\cdot c_{in}$ | `B_enc_step = B_encD[i] * B_encD_scale`<br>`rho = np.sqrt(1 - B_enc_step**2)`<br>`c = rho * c + B_enc_step * c_in` |\n",
    "        | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "\n",
    "    <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "    * **Update $M_{FC}$ to associate the item's features with the current context $c$ (governed by $\\gamma_{fc}$).**\n",
    "\n",
    "        | $\\Delta M_{FC} = \\gamma_{fc} (c_i \\cdot f_{in}^T)$<br>$M_{FC} = M_{FC} + \\Delta M_{FC}$ | `d_w_fc = gamma_fc_val * (c @ f_in.T)`<br>`net_w_fc += d_w_fc` |\n",
    "        | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "\n",
    "    <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "    * **Update $M_{CF}$ to associate the current context $c$ with the item's features.**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "        | $\\Delta M_{CF} = \\gamma_{cf} (f_{in} \\cdot c_i^T)$<br>$M_{CF} = M_{CF} + \\Delta M_{CF}$ | `d_w_cf = lrate_cf_enc * (f_in @ c.T)`<br>`net_w_cf += d_w_cf` |\n",
    "        | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "\n",
    "    ---"
   ]
