    "### Retrieval pseudocode\n",
    "* Initialize the recall list and elapsed time.\n",
    "* **While max allowable recalls isn't reached and time hasn't expired:**\n",
    "  * Use the current context $c$ to cue memory, computing the support (activations) for all items via $M_{CF}$.\n",
    "  * Mask out items that have already been recalled to prevent repetition.\n",
    "  * Check if the highest activation exceeds the retrieval threshold.\n",
    "  * **If threshold is met:**\n",
    "    * Select an item to recall using a competitive rule (e.g., softmax) based on activations.\n",
    "    * Record the recalled item and increment the simulated time.\n",
    "    * Formulate a new input context $c_{in}$ based on the recalled item's features retrieved via $M_{FC}$.\n",
    "    * Update the context vector $c$ by drifting it towards this new $c_{in}$, scaled by the retrieval drift rate ($\\eta$ or $B_{rec}$).\n",
    "  * **If threshold is NOT met:**\n",
    "    * Terminate the recall phase early."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a5d6a5de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Implementation\n",
    "* **Initialize the recall list and elapsed time.**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "    | $recalls = []$, $t = 0$ | `recalls = np.zeros(N, dtype=int)`<br>`t_sim = 0.0` |\n",
    "    | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "<br>\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "* **While max allowable recalls isn't reached and time hasn't expired:**\n",
    "    * **Use the current context $c$ to cue memory, computing the support (activations) for all items via $M_{CF}$.**\n",
    "\n",
    "        | $a = M_{CF} \\cdot c$ | `support = net_w_cf @ c` |\n",
    "        | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "    <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "    * **Mask out items that have already been recalled to prevent repetition.**\n",
    "\n",
    "        | $a[recalled\\_items] = -\\infty$ | `support[recalls[:n_recalls] - 1] = -np.inf` |\n",
    "        | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "    <br>\n",
    "    \n",
    "    > **[DIAGNOSTIC LOG: Item Evidence]**: Logged immediately after masking. Snapshots the raw activation values (`support`) of all available items to track the competition between the target and its neighbors before the softmax winner-take-all selection.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "    * **Check if the highest activation exceeds the retrieval threshold.**\n",
    "\n",
    "        | $\\max(a) \\geq \\theta$ | `if np.max(support) >= thresh:` |\n",
    "        | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "    <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "    * **If threshold is met:**\n",
    "        * **Select an item to recall using a competitive rule (e.g., softmax) based on activations.**\n",
    "\n",
    "            | $P(i) = \\frac{\\exp(a_i)}{\\sum \\exp(a_j)}$ | `p = np.exp(support) / np.sum(np.exp(support))`<br>`winner = rng.choice(..., p=p)` |\n",
    "            | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "        <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "        * **Record the recalled item and increment the simulated time.**\n",
    "        *(Standard array assignment and variable incrementing in code)*\n",
    "        <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "        * **Formulate a new input context $c_{in}$ based on the recalled item's features retrieved via $M_{FC}$.**\n",
    "\n",
    "            | $c_{in, raw} = M_{FC} \\cdot f_{rec}$<br>$c_{in} = \\frac{c_{in, raw}}{\\|c_{in, raw}\\|}$ | `c_in_raw = net_w_fc @ f_rec`<br>`c_in = c_in_raw / _norm(c_in_raw)` |\n",
    "            | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "        <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "        > **[DIAGNOSTIC LOG: FC Alignment]**: Logged immediately after calculating `c_in_raw`. Compares the current context vector $c$ with the newly retrieved input context $c_{in, raw}$ (via dot product/cosine similarity) to measure how much the context is about to \"shift\".\n",
    "\n",
    "        <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "        * **Update the context vector $c$ by drifting it towards this new $c_{in}$, scaled by the retrieval drift rate ($\\eta$ or $\\beta_{rec}$).**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "            | $\\rho = \\sqrt{1 - \\beta_{rec}^2}$<br>$c_t = \\rho \\cdot c_{t-1} + \\beta_{rec} \\cdot c_{in}$ | `rho = np.sqrt(1 - B_rec**2)`<br>`c = rho * c + B_rec * c_in` |\n",
    "            | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "        <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "        > **[DIAGNOSTIC LOG: Context Trace]**: Logged immediately after the context vector is updated. Saves the exact numerical state of $c$ to track how the model's internal representation traverses through the semantic/episodic space over the course of the recall period.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    <br>\n",
    "        \n",
    "\n",
    "    * **If threshold is NOT met:**\n",
    "        * **Terminate the recall phase early (model \"gives up\").**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "            | Break loop | `else: break` |\n",
    "            | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "        <br>\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
