    "### Batch Simulation Wrappers\n",
    "\n",
    "These functions wrap `simulate_single_trial` to run `n_sims` independent trials. They structure the output into standardized 2D arrays (`(N, n_sims)`) for behavioral analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Function | Purpose | Returns | Overhead |\n",
    "| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
    "| `run_simulation` | Standard batch execution for behavioral sweeps. | `recall_sims`, `times_sims`, final `net_w_fc`, final `net_w_cf` | Low (Optimized for speed) |\n",
    "| `run_simulation_with_diagnostics` | Batch execution with deep internal tracking. | Same as above + `all_diagnostics` (List of dicts per trial) | High (Memory/Compute intensive) |"
